{
  "_comment": [
    "The authored half of the CLI reference. Everything else on that page is",
    "read out of the binary's own help, and this is the part no introspection",
    "can produce: what a flag is for, and whether the command refuses to run",
    "without it.",
    "",
    "Required is stated here rather than read from the source because the tree",
    "spells it three ways - requireAll(notGiven(...)), a bare empty-string",
    "check, and a requireAll that only applies once another flag was given, as",
    "basemap's area does. A regular expression that read all three would call",
    "basemap's edges required, which they are not: without -layer it lists the",
    "layers and stops.",
    "",
    "A flag with no entry here fails the generator, which is the point: a flag",
    "nobody decided a purpose for is a flag that lands in the reference",
    "unexplained."
  ],
  "purposes": {
    "capture": "capture and scripting: it reaches a view, a panel or a menu without a click, so a screenshot or a script does not need a hand on the mouse. None of these changes a result.",
    "data": "where the inputs come from, and whether the network may be used to get them. Nothing here is part of the physics.",
    "diagnostic": "measures the application itself rather than the network it is simulating.",
    "output": "where the answer is written and how much of it is said. It does not change what was computed.",
    "result": "an input the answer depends on. Change it and the number changes."
  },
